---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import bitPerfect from '../assets/screenshots/bit-perfect.png';
---
<section class="sec">
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="split-copy">
      <h2>Bit-perfect, when the output allows.</h2>
      <p>
        TIDE switches your device to the track’s sample rate, so nothing is
        resampled. No exclusive mode, so other apps still play.
      </p>
      <ul class="tiers">
        <li><span class="dot q-max"></span><strong class="q-max">MAX</strong> Up to 24-bit / 192 kHz FLAC</li>
        <li><span class="dot q-high"></span><strong class="q-high">HIGH</strong> 16-bit / 44.1 kHz FLAC</li>
        <li><span class="dot q-low"></span><strong class="q-low">LOW</strong> AAC, for slow connections</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="fine">Tap the quality pill to see the signal path, and why it is or isn’t bit-perfect.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="signal-shot">
      <Picture
        src={bitPerfect}
        formats={['avif', 'webp']}
        widths={[420, 840]}
        sizes="(max-width: 468px) calc(100vw - 48px), 420px"
        alt="TIDE signal path popup: a 24-bit 48 kHz FLAC source, sample rate conversion to 44.1 kHz, and MacBook Pro speakers, with the bit-perfect playback toggle"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="dsp">
  <div class="container split split-rev">
    <div class="tile eq">
      <div class="term-bar">
        <span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
        <span>DSP · Headphones</span>
      </div>
      <div class="eq-body">
